.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt INIT 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm init
.Nd RavenBSD PID 1 service manager
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
program is the first user process started by the kernel.
It maps the boot archive from handle 1 and reads the service manifests under
.Pa /etc/services.d/ .
Each manifest is a small TOML file with the service name, executable, arguments,
environment, dependencies, restart policy and readiness mode.
.Pp
Services start in dependency order computed at boot.
When the initfs contains the storage chain
.Pq Pa blockd , fsd-ufs , vfsd ,
.Nm
uses two phases.  Phase 1 starts only the bootstrap closure of
.Pa logd , initfsd , ramfsd , nulld , zerod , randd , blockd , fsd-ufs , vfsd
and their dependencies (including the device servers).
Once
.Dq ufs:
and
.Dq file:
are up, it mounts the UFS root through
.Xr vfsd 8
at
.Pa /root
and reads the root manifests from
.Pa /root/etc/services.d
and
.Pa /root/etc/rc.conf .
Root manifests replace a bootstrap manifest with the same name in place and add the rest; the
dependency plan is recomputed and phase 2 starts every service that has not started yet.
A root executable is read from
.Pa /root Ns Ar exec ;
when that file is absent the service falls back to its initfs executable and logs the reason.
This is a
.Pa /root
prefix, not a second root mount: vfsd keeps its one
.Pa /
mount.
.Pp
Profiles without the storage chain keep the one-phase initfs plan.  The
.Pa hw
profile uses release user programs and an 8 MiB UFS root image; until the virtio-blk driver lands,
blockd serves that image from the initfs RAM disk.
.Pp
A missing dependency or a dependency cycle is fatal:
.Nm
prints
.Dq svcd: <reason>
and exits 1.
A malformed manifest is reported as
.Dq svcd: <file>: <error>
and that service is skipped; if another service needs it, the missing dependency
is fatal.
.Pp
.Nm
prints
.Dq svcd: <name> up
when a service is ready,
.Dq svcd: <name> failed: <reason>
when readiness times out, and
.Dq svcd: all services up
once every required service (or a service with a restart policy other than
.Dq never )
is running.
A service that exits is restarted according to
.Va restart ,
.Va restart_delay_ms ,
.Va max_restarts
and
.Va window_ms .
When the crash-loop limit is reached,
.Nm
prints
.Dq svcd: <name> crash loop, giving up
and stops restarting it.
.Pp
.Nm
registers the
.Dq svc:
scheme.
Its directory lists the services and
.Pa svc:/<name>
returns one status line
.Dq <name> <state> <pid-or-handle> <restarts> .
See
.Xr svcctl 1 .
.Pp
When no service manifests are present,
.Nm
keeps the M1 behaviour: it prints
.Dq init: starting ,
the
.Xr uname 1
line and
.Dq init: done ,
then exits 0.
.Pp
Test mode is configured by
.Pa /etc/svcd.conf :
.Bl -tag -width "exit_when_settled"
.It Cm exit_when_exits No = Ar service
Exit with that service's status as soon as it terminates.
.It Cm exit_when_settled No = true
Once every service has started and no one-shot work is still starting or restarting, print
.Dq svcd: settled
and exit 0 if no required service failed, otherwise 1.
Long-running services are not required to stop first; the process-wide exit terminates their
workers.
.El
Unknown keys are reported as
.Dq svcd: /etc/svcd.conf: unknown key <key>
and ignored.
The normal profile has no such file, so
.Nm
runs forever.
.Pp
.Dq STOP
terminates the service process with the authorized termination primitive, waits for its terminal
state and only then reports success; the service scheme name is released by that teardown.
.Dq RESTART
performs the stop first and starts the replacement only after the old process is gone.
The process-wide exit also terminates the
.Dq svc:
server and every worker still blocked in
.Dv PROC_WAIT , so no helper thread keeps
.Nm
alive or the console open.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/*.toml
Service manifests.
.It Pa /etc/rc.conf
Optional
.Dq NAME_enable
and
.Dq NAME_restart
overrides.
.It Pa /root/etc/services.d/*.toml
Root-filesystem service manifests (two-phase boot).
.It Pa /root/etc/rc.conf
Root-filesystem overrides applied to the merged service set.
.It Pa /etc/svcd.conf
Optional test-mode settings.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Nm
exits non-zero when the initfs, a manifest, the dependency graph or the
.Dq svc:
scheme cannot be initialised, or when a test-mode setting asks for a failure
exit.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr svcctl 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
